   },
   {
    "id": "p_00052",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The POSIX.1-1990 standard was silent with regard to the behavior of [I51]rmdir[/I51]() when there are multiple hard links to the\ndirectory being removed. The requirement to set [I52]errno[/I52] to [EEXIST] or [ENOTEMPTY] clarifies the behavior in this case.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I51": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I52": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00053",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     7
    ],
    "text": "If the current working directory of the process is being removed, that should be an allowed error.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00054",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     9
    ],
    "text": "Virtually all existing implementations detect [ENOTEMPTY] or the case of dot-dot. The text in [A53][I54]2.3 Error Numbers[/I54][/A53] about returning any one of the possible errors permits that\nbehavior to continue. The [ELOOP] error may be returned if more than {SYMLOOP_MAX} symbolic links are encountered during resolution\nof the [I55]path[/I55] argument.",
    "placeholders": {
     "A53": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/V2_chap02.html#tag_16_03\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I54": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I55": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
